WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.271
All night on the fire.

00:00:01.281 --> 00:00:02.577
Still not cooked.

00:00:02.587 --> 00:00:05.981
Charles Darwin, in the Andes, 1835.

00:00:05.991 --> 00:00:08.444
The water boiled, yet his potatoes stayed

00:00:08.454 --> 00:00:09.923
nearly as hard as ever.

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.117
His two companions blamed the pot.

00:00:12.127 --> 00:00:13.140
It was new.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.457
Darwin knew the culprit:

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:15.344
thin air.

00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:17.807
Up there, water boils below 100 degrees

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.787
Celsius.

00:00:18.797 --> 00:00:20.955
A pressure cooker does the reverse:

00:00:20.965 --> 00:00:24.005
trapped steam lifts boiling to about 121

00:00:24.015 --> 00:00:25.065
Celsius.
